  "red": {
    "$description": "The error colour, chosen 2026-08-29 from a lab of six drawn on the two surfaces that paint it. Candidate C: one step louder than the brand amber (chroma 0.145 against amber's 0.114) and 41 degrees from it. The volume is the whole decision \u2014 what shipped before was shadcn's default at chroma 0.239, 2.1x louder than anything else in the design, which is what made it read as somebody else's rather than the hue. Declared in sRGB rather than oklch because Terrazzo round-trips oklch through another space and comes back at a different value.",
    "01": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": {
        "colorSpace": "srgb",
        "components": [0.72549, 0.2902, 0.25098]
      },
      "$extensions": {
        "mode": {
          "dark": {
            "colorSpace": "srgb",
            "components": [0.9098, 0.48627, 0.45098]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "green": {
    "$description": "SIGNED IN, and nothing else. The design adds #4a8a52 to the palette for one purpose: the dot beside the account name in the nav rail. It is the only binary state in the app that is not amber's \u201cnon-default\u201d job \u2014 an account is not a choice you made about a skill \u2014 so it cannot borrow the accent, and grey would say nothing at all. The dark value is lifted by the same amount red-01's is (+47/+50/+51 in 0-255 channels), which is what keeps a small 5px square legible on #161513 rather than reading as a hole.",
    "01": {
      "$type": "color",
      "$value": {
        "colorSpace": "srgb",
        "components": [0.2902, 0.54118, 0.32157]
      },
      "$extensions": {
        "mode": {
          "dark": {
            "colorSpace": "srgb",
            "components": [0.47451, 0.73725, 0.52157]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
